IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja1-part2-hearings.l4: Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- LAYER 1, Part 2, ss 8 (sittings in private) and 8A (hearing through electronic means of communication). The source is a plain-text rendering, not the official text.
-- Every name begins with the section it implements. Imports the keel's `scja-core` only.
-- A judgment the text leaves to the court ("if the court is satisfied") is a plain input, never guessed. The Broadcasting Act 1994, the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974,
-- the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016, the Evidence Act 1893 and the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 are not among the sources: what they define is asked as a fact.

§ `Part 2: The Supreme Court (continued)`

§§ `Section 8: Sittings in private`

-- s 8(1). Deeming: the place in which a court is held to try a cause or matter is an open and public court.
-- src:521 | 8.—(1) The place in which any court is held for the purpose of
-- src:522 | trying any cause or matter, civil or criminal, is deemed an open and
-- src:523 | public court to which the public generally may have access.
@ref s 8(1) (src:521-523)
GIVEN `the place is where a court is held for trying a cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the place in which a court is held to try a cause or matter, civil or criminal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) the place is deemed an open and public court to which the public generally may have access` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the place is where a court is held for trying a cause or matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming speaks of "the place in which any court is held for the purpose of trying any cause or matter"

-- The grounds s 8(2) names (and s 8(2A), (6)): the Act's list of what makes a private hearing expedient.
DECLARE `s 8(2) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 8(2) the interests of justice`
    `s 8(2) public safety`
    `s 8(2) public security`
    `s 8(2) propriety`
    `s 8(2) the national interest of Singapore`
    `s 8(2) the national security of Singapore`
    `s 8(2) other sufficient reason`

-- s 8(2). Plain gloss: may the court hear this in private? Only if the court is satisfied that it is expedient on one of the grounds; "satisfied" is the court's judgment, asked as a fact.
-- src:525 | (2) The court has power to hear any matter or proceeding or any
-- src:526 | part thereof in private if the court is satisfied that it is expedient in the
-- src:527 | interests of justice, public safety, public security or propriety, the
-- src:528 | national interest or national security of Singapore, or for other
-- src:529 | sufficient reason to do so.
@ref s 8(2) (src:525-529)
GIVEN `the grounds on which the court is satisfied it is expedient to hear the matter in private` IS A LIST OF `s 8(2) ground` @desc On which of these grounds is the court satisfied that it is expedient to hear the matter or proceeding, or part of it, in private?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) the court has power to hear the matter or proceeding in private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF count `the grounds on which the court is satisfied it is expedient to hear the matter in private` AT LEAST 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied that it is expedient"

-- s 8(2AA). An application, on the ground of national interest or national security, for a matter to be held in private is to be heard in private.
-- src:535 | (2AA) Any application for a matter or proceeding to be held in
-- src:536 | private, on the grounds that it is expedient in the national interest or
-- src:537 | national security of Singapore to do so, is to be heard in private.
@ref s 8(2AA) (src:535-537)
GIVEN `the application is for a matter to be held in private on the ground of the national interest or national security of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one for a matter or proceeding to be held in private on the ground that it is expedient in the national interest or national security of Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2AA) the application is to be heard in private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is for a matter to be held in private on the ground of the national interest or national security of Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any application ... on the grounds that it is expedient in the national interest or national security of Singapore"

-- s 8(2AB). The court may hear such an application, or part, otherwise than in private if satisfied of both (a) and (b).
-- src:541 | (2AB) The court has the power to hear any application mentioned
-- src:542 | in subsection (2AA), or any part of such an application, otherwise
-- src:543 | than in private, if the court is satisfied that —
-- src:550 | (a) it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the
-- src:551 | application or part of the application otherwise than in
-- src:552 | private; and
-- src:554 | (b) it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national
-- src:555 | security of Singapore to hear the application or part of the
-- src:556 | application otherwise than in private.
@ref s 8(2AB) (src:541-556)
GIVEN `it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application otherwise than in private` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application, or the part, otherwise than in private?
      `it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security to hear it otherwise than in private` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore to hear the application, or the part, otherwise than in private?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2AB) the court has power to hear the application otherwise than in private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application otherwise than in private`
           AND `it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security to hear it otherwise than in private` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied that (a) ... and (b)"

-- Gathering by hand (ruling E1, option B as guidance): ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB) together. The application is to be heard in private unless the court has the power in 8(2AB);
-- where it has the power the Act does not say whether it will use it, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F5). Not a new rule: it calls the two rules above.
-- src:535 | (2AA) Any application for a matter or proceeding to be held in
-- src:536 | private, on the grounds that it is expedient in the national interest or
-- src:537 | national security of Singapore to do so, is to be heard in private.
-- src:541 | (2AB) The court has the power to hear any application mentioned
-- src:542 | in subsection (2AA), or any part of such an application, otherwise
-- src:543 | than in private, if the court is satisfied that —
-- src:550 | (a) it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the
-- src:551 | application or part of the application otherwise than in
-- src:552 | private; and
-- src:554 | (b) it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national
-- src:555 | security of Singapore to hear the application or part of the
-- src:556 | application otherwise than in private.
@ref ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB) together (src:535-556)
GIVEN `the application is for a matter to be held in private on the ground of the national interest or national security of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application otherwise than in private` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security to hear it otherwise than in private` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB) the application will be heard in private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 8(2AA) the application is to be heard in private` `the application is for a matter to be held in private on the ground of the national interest or national security of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 8(2AA) speaks of applications on the ground of national interest or national security
        IF `s 8(2AB) the court has power to hear the application otherwise than in private` `it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application otherwise than in private` `it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security to hear it otherwise than in private` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the court has the power to hear it otherwise than in private and the Act does not say whether it uses it
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- What s 8(2A) lets the court order removed or redacted from a court document intended to be produced before the court.
DECLARE `s 8(2A) thing in a court document` IS ONE OF
    `s 8(2A)(a) the name, address or photograph of a witness`
    `s 8(2A)(b) evidence or another thing likely to lead to the identification of such a witness by a person other than a party`
    `s 8(2A)(c) information that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore`
    `s 8(2A) another thing`

-- s 8(2A). Plain gloss: may the court order this removed or redacted? The court must be satisfied it is expedient (interests of justice, public safety, public security, propriety,
-- national interest or national security, or other sufficient reason); the thing must be one of (a) to (c), contained in a court document intended to be produced before the court.
-- src:560 | (2A) A court may, in any matter or proceeding or any part thereof
-- src:561 | tried or held or to be tried or held before it, if satisfied that it is
-- src:562 | expedient in the interests of justice, public safety, public security or
-- src:563 | propriety, the national interest or national security of Singapore, or
-- src:564 | for other sufficient reason to do so, order that —
-- src:566 | (a) the name, address or photograph of any witness;
-- src:570 | (b) any evidence or any other thing likely to lead to the
-- src:571 | identification of such witness by a person other than the
-- src:572 | party to that matter or proceeding; or
-- src:576 | (c) any information that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the
-- src:577 | national interest or national security of Singapore,
-- src:579 | which is contained in any court document intended to be produced
-- src:580 | before the court, be removed or be sufficiently redacted.
@ref s 8(2A) (src:560-580)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 8(2A) thing in a court document` @desc Which of these is it: (a) a witness's name, address or photograph; (b) evidence or another thing likely to lead to the identification of such a witness by someone other than a party; (c) information that may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security; or another thing?
      `it is contained in a court document intended to be produced before the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it contained in a court document that is intended to be produced before the court?
      `the court is satisfied that it is expedient to order its removal or redaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is expedient, in the interests of justice, public safety, public security or propriety, the national interest or national security, or for other sufficient reason, to order it removed or redacted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2A) the court has power to order the thing removed or sufficiently redacted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is satisfied that it is expedient to order its removal or redaction` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if satisfied that it is expedient"
        IF thing EQUALS `s 8(2A) another thing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order is for "(a) ... (b) ... or (c)"
        IF `it is contained in a court document intended to be produced before the court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which is contained in any court document intended to be produced before the court"

-- What a s 8(3) order may forbid.
DECLARE `s 8(3) act the order may forbid` IS ONE OF
    `s 8(3)(a) publishing the name, address or photograph of a witness, or evidence or another thing likely to lead to the identification of such a witness`
    `s 8(3)(b) doing another act likely to lead to the identification of such a witness`
    `s 8(3)(c) publishing information relating to the matter that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore`
    `s 8(3) another act`

-- s 8(3). Plain gloss: may the court order that no person is to do this? At any time; for the three kinds the section names.
-- src:586 | (3) A court may at any time order that no person is to —
-- src:588 | (a) publish the name, address or photograph of any witness in
-- src:589 | any matter or proceeding or any part thereof tried or held or
-- src:590 | to be tried or held before it, or any evidence or any other
-- src:591 | thing likely to lead to the identification of any such
-- src:592 | witness;
-- src:596 | (b) do any other act which is likely to lead to the identification
-- src:597 | of any witness mentioned in paragraph (a); or
-- src:608 | (c) publish any information relating to any matter or
-- src:609 | proceeding before the court that, if disclosed, may be
-- src:610 | prejudicial to the national interest or national security of
-- src:611 | Singapore.
@ref s 8(3) (src:586-611)
GIVEN act IS A `s 8(3) act the order may forbid` @desc What would the order forbid: (a) publishing a witness's name, address or photograph or identifying evidence; (b) another act likely to identify such a witness; (c) publishing information that may prejudice the national interest or national security; or another act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the court may order that no person is to do the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 8(3)(a) publishing the name, address or photograph of a witness, or evidence or another thing likely to lead to the identification of such a witness` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 8(3)(b) doing another act likely to lead to the identification of such a witness` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 8(3)(c) publishing information relating to the matter that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names three acts and does not say "only"

-- s 8(4). The offence of contravening an order under s 8(2A) or (3), and its ceilings ("not exceeding"): $5,000, 3 years, or both.
-- src:615 | (4) Any person who acts in contravention of any order under
-- src:616 | subsection (2A) or (3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable
-- src:617 | on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:618 | term not exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 8(4) (src:615-618)
`s 8(4) the highest fine` MEANS 5000
`s 8(4) the longest imprisonment, in years` MEANS 3

@ref s 8(4) any person who acts in contravention (src:615-616)
GIVEN `the person acted in contravention of an order under section 8(2A) or 8(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person act in contravention of an order made under section 8(2A) or 8(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person acted in contravention of an order under section 8(2A) or 8(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who acts in contravention of any order under subsection (2A) or (3)"

@ref s 8(4) liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both (src:616-618)
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER @desc What fine (in dollars) is in question? Use 0 if none.
      `years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years of imprisonment? Use 0 if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4) the sentence is within what the person is liable to on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF fine AT MOST `s 8(4) the highest fine` AND `years of imprisonment` AT MOST `s 8(4) the longest imprisonment, in years` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both"

-- Who s 8(5) lets the court permit to be present when it hears a matter in private.
DECLARE `s 8(5) individual` IS ONE OF
    `s 8(5)(a) a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service`
    `s 8(5)(b) an individual the court determines has a sufficient interest in the matter or proceeding`
    `s 8(5)(c) any other individual that the court specifies in the particular case`
    `s 8(5) another individual`

-- s 8(5). Plain gloss: may the court, in its discretion, let this person be present while it hears the matter in private? Only a court that hears the matter, or a part of it, in private may.
-- src:622 | (5) A court that hears the whole or any part of any matter or
-- src:623 | proceeding in private may, in its discretion, permit any of the
-- src:624 | following individuals to be present in the courtroom while that matter
-- src:625 | or proceeding is heard in private:
-- src:627 | (a) any journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a
-- src:628 | broadcasting service;
-- src:630 | (b) any individual whom the court determines has a sufficient
-- src:631 | interest in that matter or proceeding;
-- src:633 | (c) any other individual that the court specifies in any
-- src:634 | particular case.
@ref s 8(5) (src:622-634)
GIVEN individual IS A `s 8(5) individual` @desc Is the person: (a) a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service; (b) someone the court has determined has a sufficient interest in the matter; (c) another individual the court specifies in this case; or another individual?
      `the court hears the whole or a part of the matter in private` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court hear the whole or any part of the matter or proceeding in private?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(5) the court may permit the individual to be present in the courtroom` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court hears the whole or a part of the matter in private` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that hears the whole or any part of any matter or proceeding in private may"
        IF individual EQUALS `s 8(5) another individual` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraphs name three kinds of individual; (c) leaves the rest to the court's specification in the case
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The matters s 8(6) lists as ones the court may consider.
DECLARE `s 8(6) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 8(6)(a) whether the defence of an accused person will be prejudiced by the presence of a member of the public in the courtroom`
    `s 8(6)(b) whether an accused person or witness has a legitimate interest in privacy that needs to be protected`
    `s 8(6)(c) whether the object of the matter or proceeding will be defeated by publicity if it is heard in open court`
    `s 8(6)(d) whether an accused person or witness has a legitimate interest in protecting the confidentiality of information that may be disclosed`
    `s 8(6)(e) whether information that may be disclosed will be prejudicial to the interests of Singapore`
    `s 8(6) another matter`

-- s 8(6). Plain gloss: is this a matter the court may consider in deciding whether to hear a matter in private? "include": the five are named and the list is not closed.
-- src:640 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (2), the matters that the court
-- src:641 | may consider, when deciding whether it is expedient in the interests
-- src:642 | of justice, public safety, public security or propriety, the national
-- src:643 | interest or national security of Singapore, or for other sufficient
-- src:644 | reason, to hear the whole or any part of any matter or proceeding in
-- src:645 | private, include the following matters:
-- src:647 | (a) whether the defence of any accused person in that matter or
-- src:648 | proceeding will be prejudiced by the presence of any
-- src:649 | member of the public in the courtroom;
-- src:651 | (b) whether any accused person or witness in that matter or
-- src:652 | proceeding has any legitimate interest in privacy that needs
-- src:653 | to be protected;
-- src:660 | (c) whether the object of that matter or proceeding will be
-- src:661 | defeated by publicity if that matter or proceeding is heard
-- src:662 | in open court;
-- src:664 | (d) whether any accused person or witness in that matter or
-- src:665 | proceeding has any legitimate interest in protecting the
-- src:666 | confidentiality of any information that may be disclosed
-- src:667 | during the hearing of that matter or proceeding;
-- src:669 | (e) whether any information that may be disclosed during the
-- src:670 | hearing of that matter or proceeding will be prejudicial to
-- src:671 | the interests of Singapore.
@ref s 8(6) (src:640-671)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 8(6) matter` @desc Which matter is in question: (a) the accused's defence being prejudiced by the public's presence; (b) a legitimate interest in privacy; (c) the object of the matter being defeated by publicity; (d) a legitimate interest in the confidentiality of information; (e) information prejudicial to the interests of Singapore; or another matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(6) the court may consider the matter in deciding whether to hear in private` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 8(6) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the matters that the court may consider ... include the following matters"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 8(7). "broadcasting service" and "newspaper" have the meanings given by the Broadcasting Act 1994 s 2(1) and the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974 s 2(1), neither of which is among the sources:
-- the answer is the borrowed fact the person states.
-- src:679 | “broadcasting service” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of
-- src:680 | the Broadcasting Act 1994;
@ref s 8(7) “broadcasting service” (src:679-680)
