GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7) broadcasting service: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Broadcasting Act 1994` MEANS
    JUST `it is a broadcasting service within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Broadcasting Act 1994`

-- src:682 | “newspaper” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
-- src:683 | Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974.
@ref s 8(7) “newspaper” (src:682-683)
GIVEN `it is a newspaper within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a newspaper within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7) newspaper: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974` MEANS
    JUST `it is a newspaper within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974`

-- s 8(5)(a). Plain gloss: is this person a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service, in the Acts' senses? Calls the two s 8(7) rules.
-- src:627 | (a) any journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a
-- src:628 | broadcasting service;
@ref s 8(5)(a) any journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service (src:627-628)
GIVEN `the person is a journalist and reports news` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a journalist who reports news?
      `reports for a newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person report for a newspaper within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974?
      `reports for a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person report for a broadcasting service within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Broadcasting Act 1994?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(5)(a) the individual is a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a journalist and reports news`
           AND (`s 8(7) newspaper: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974` `reports for a newspaper` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                OR `s 8(7) broadcasting service: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Broadcasting Act 1994` `reports for a broadcasting service` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a person who is not such a journalist may still be within (b) or (c)

§§ `Section 8A: Court may conduct hearing through electronic means of communication`

-- s 8A(1). Plain gloss: may the court conduct this hearing by this electronic means? Not a matter prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules.
-- A live video, television or audio link, or any other electronic means approved by the Chief Justice. "(other than ...)" is read as the text's no (question QE; fork F6).
-- src:691 | 8A.—(1) Without limiting section 8, the court may conduct the
-- src:692 | hearing of any matter or proceeding (other than a matter or
-- src:693 | proceeding prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice
-- src:694 | Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules) through a live video link, a
-- src:695 | live television link, a live audio link or any other electronic means of
-- src:696 | communication approved by the Chief Justice.
@ref s 8A(1) (src:691-696)
GIVEN `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules prescribe as outside electronic hearings?
      `how the hearing is conducted` IS A `Manner of hearing` @desc How would the hearing be conducted: through a live video link, a live television link, a live audio link only, or some other way?
      `another electronic means approved by the Chief Justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it conducted through some other electronic means of communication that the Chief Justice has approved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than a matter or proceeding prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules)"
        IF `how the hearing is conducted` EQUALS `through a live video link` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `how the hearing is conducted` EQUALS `through a live television link` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `how the hearing is conducted` EQUALS `through a live audio link only` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `another electronic means approved by the Chief Justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names the means it allows and says "any other electronic means ... approved by the Chief Justice"; other ways of hearing are for other provisions

