@ref s 8A(2) (src:700-703)
GIVEN `the provision is section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016, section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893 or section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016, section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893 or section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(2) section 8A(1) affects the operation of the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision is section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016, section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893 or section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the operation of"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 8A(2) names three provisions

-- s 8A(3). The prohibition on a part of a hearing through a live audio link only, with no accompanying live video or television link. It applies "where" any of (a), (b), (c) holds;
-- a "where" that is not met is a no (ruling of 2026-11-05). A hearing not through an audio link only is outside the prohibition (a scope limit: NOTHING).
-- src:714 | (3) A court must not conduct any part of a hearing of a matter
-- src:715 | through a live audio link only, without an accompanying live video
-- src:716 | link or live television link —
-- src:718 | (a) where oral evidence is given during that part of the hearing
-- src:719 | (including in a trial of an offence) in a criminal proceeding;
-- src:721 | (b) where oral evidence is given during that part of the hearing
-- src:722 | (including in a trial of an action) in a civil proceeding,
-- src:723 | unless all the parties consent; or
-- src:725 | (c) where the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court, the
-- src:726 | Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules.
@ref s 8A(3) (src:714-726)
GIVEN hearing IS A Hearing
      `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (hearing's `manner of hearing` EQUALS `through a live audio link only`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "through a live audio link only, without an accompanying live video link or live television link"
        IF `s 8A(3)(a) a criminal proceeding where oral evidence is given` hearing THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 8A(3)(b) a civil proceeding where oral evidence is given and the parties do not all consent` hearing THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules` THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where" (a), (b) or (c) is not met

@ref s 8A(3)(a) (src:718-719)
GIVEN hearing IS A Hearing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8A(3)(a) a criminal proceeding where oral evidence is given` MEANS
    hearing's `nature of the proceeding` EQUALS `a criminal proceeding` AND hearing's `oral evidence is given in this part of the hearing`

@ref s 8A(3)(b) (src:721-723)
GIVEN hearing IS A Hearing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8A(3)(b) a civil proceeding where oral evidence is given and the parties do not all consent` MEANS
    hearing's `nature of the proceeding` EQUALS `a civil proceeding`
    AND hearing's `oral evidence is given in this part of the hearing`
    AND NOT hearing's `all the parties consent`

-- s 8A(3) as a regulative rule (ruling N2: the prohibition is derived from the decision above). The bearer is "A court". Run with #TRACE in the tests.
DECLARE `s 8A(3) party` IS ONE OF `s 8A(3) the court`
DECLARE `s 8A(3) act` IS ONE OF `s 8A(3) conducts the part through a live audio link only`

@ref s 8A(3) A court must not conduct any part of a hearing of a matter through a live audio link only (src:714-716)
GIVEN hearing IS A Hearing
      `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 8A(3) party` `s 8A(3) act`
`s 8A(3) the court shall not conduct the part through a live audio link only` MEANS
    IF `s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` hearing `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `s 8A(3) the court`
         SHANT `s 8A(3) conducts the part through a live audio link only`
         WITHIN 1
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 8A(3): a court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 8A(4). A temporary, insignificant disruption of the accompanying video or television link, that did not affect the court's duty to conduct proceedings fairly, is not by itself
-- conducting a part through an audio link only. "by reason only of" is a limit in the section's own words: where the three facts do not all hold the Act does not say.
-- src:730 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), a court is not considered to
-- src:731 | have conducted a part of a hearing of a matter through a live audio
-- src:732 | link only and without an accompanying live video link or live
-- src:733 | television link, by reason only of a temporary disruption in the
-- src:734 | accompanying live video link or live television link that was
-- src:735 | insignificant and which did not affect the court’s duty to conduct
-- src:736 | proceedings fairly.
@ref s 8A(4) (src:730-736)
GIVEN `the only reason is a temporary disruption in the accompanying live video or television link` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason the court was without a video or television link a temporary disruption in the accompanying live video link or live television link?
      `the disruption was insignificant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disruption insignificant?
      `the disruption did not affect the court's duty to conduct proceedings fairly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the disruption leave the court's duty to conduct proceedings fairly unaffected?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part through a live audio link only` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the only reason is a temporary disruption in the accompanying live video or television link`
           AND `the disruption was insignificant`
           AND `the disruption did not affect the court's duty to conduct proceedings fairly` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not considered to have conducted a part of a hearing of a matter through a live audio link only"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only of a temporary disruption ... that was insignificant and which did not affect the court's duty"

-- s 8A(5). The court must not conduct a hearing under s 8A(1) if that would be inconsistent with its duty to ensure the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties. An "if" that is not met is a no.
-- src:740 | (5) A court must not conduct a hearing of a matter or proceeding in
-- src:741 | the manner provided under subsection (1), if to do so would be
-- src:742 | inconsistent with the court’s duty to ensure that the hearing is
-- src:743 | conducted fairly to all parties.
@ref s 8A(5) (src:740-743)
GIVEN `to conduct it this way would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would conducting the hearing through electronic means be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that it is conducted fairly to all parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(5) the court must not conduct the hearing in the manner provided under section 8A(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `to conduct it this way would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty"

-- s 8A(6). A court conducting a hearing under s 8A(1) is deemed to be sitting at the place appointed under s 11(1) (General Division) or ss 34(1)(a) and 52(1)(a) (Appellate Division and Court of Appeal),
-- wherever the Judge or Registrar actually is. "when" is read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05). Seam 11 of PLAN.md: the Appellate Division / Court of Appeal answer comes from scja2.
-- src:747 | (6) A court is deemed to be sitting at a place appointed under
-- src:748 | section 11(1), 34(1)(a) or 52(1)(a) (as the case may be) when the
-- src:749 | court conducts a hearing of a matter or proceeding in the manner
-- src:750 | provided under subsection (1) (whether any Judge or Registrar sitting
-- src:751 | in the court is situated in Singapore or outside Singapore).
@ref s 8A(6) (src:747-751)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court conducts the hearing in the manner provided under section 8A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court conducting the hearing through a live video, television or audio link or other approved electronic means?
      `s 11(1) the place is one the Chief Justice appointed for the General Division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 34(1)(a) or s 52(1)(a) the place is one the Chief Justice appointed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at the appointed place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court conducts the hearing in the manner provided under section 8A(1)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the court conducts a hearing of a matter or proceeding in the manner provided under subsection (1)"
        IF court EQUALS `General Division` THEN `s 11(1) the place is one the Chief Justice appointed for the General Division`
        IF court EQUALS `Appellate Division` THEN `s 34(1)(a) or s 52(1)(a) the place is one the Chief Justice appointed`
        IF court EQUALS `Court of Appeal` THEN `s 34(1)(a) or s 52(1)(a) the place is one the Chief Justice appointed`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 8A(6) names the places appointed under ss 11(1), 34(1)(a) and 52(1)(a), for the courts they govern
